ANTI-LEAKAGE — TREAT THIS AS A PRODUCT PROBLEM, NOT A POLICY PROBLEM
This category is the worst case for leakage: high-value repeat transactions
between the same two parties. Service marketplaces commonly lose a large share
of potential revenue this way. Enforcement will not save us. Value will.
Make Pay-on-TradeBook worth more than the fee it costs:
  - Payout to the vendor within 24 hours of completion. Faster than a check.
  - Auto-generated invoice, year-end 1099 totals, both sides.
  - Custody log and POD attached to the payment — the document a director wants
    when something goes wrong six months later.
  - Dispute record. Handshake jobs get none of this.
Keep "We'll settle direct" available and honest. Track its rate weekly.
If leakage passes 40%, the answer is to raise Pay-on-TradeBook's value or lower
the fee — never to hide vendor contact info. Directors will not tolerate that
and it would confirm the "lead desk" fear.

