MACROS

Does cheapest win?
"No. On urgent work the first vendor to accept takes it and you confirm — you
see the price and ETA first and you can decline. On scheduled work you see
price, arrival, and on-site or mail-in together and you click Award on the one
you want. The book never picks for you."

What does it cost?
"Right now it's free on both sides while we fill the book. Funeral homes stay
free permanently. Vendors will be $29 a month or $290 a year later on; the
first 25 vendors lock $149 for year two. If you pay through TradeBook there's
a 10% book fee, minimum $15, maximum $150 — and you can always settle direct
for nothing."

Why should I pay through the app?
"Payout in 24 hours, invoice generated for you, year-end totals for both sides,
and the custody log and proof of delivery attached to the payment. If something
goes sideways six months later, that record is the whole reason."

I don't want to pay on TradeBook
"Then use We'll settle direct. No book fee. The job still shows awarded and you
still get the record."

Vendor has not connected payouts
"The job still stands. Pay-on-TradeBook waits until they finish Stripe Connect.
We email them. Handshake is available if you'd rather settle direct."

Why do you need my license and insurance?
"Because a director who's never used you is deciding at 2 a.m. whether to hand
you a body. The badge is what makes that a yes. We verify the documents; we
don't guarantee the work, and we say so plainly in the terms."

Refund
"Before payout lands: request it on the job. After payout: email
support@tradebook.co with the job ID. We do not hold remains and we do not
guarantee workmanship. We reverse the book payment when the facts support it."

